items.prompt:
Given a Python dictionary as input, write a program that converts it into a JSON string. The input dictionary may contain nested dictionaries and lists. The input will be given as a single line, representing a Python dictionary. Your program should read the input, convert it to a JSON string, and print the result.

Input Format:
A single line representing a Python dictionary, for example: {"name": "John", "age": 30, "children": [{"name": "Jane", "age": 10}]}

Output Format:
A single line containing the JSON string representation of the input dictionary.

Example
Input
{"name": "John", "age": 30, "children": [{"name": "Jane", "age": 10}]}

Output
{"name": "John", "age": 30, "children": [{"name": "Jane", "age": 10}]}
